# The controller image copies only the Go module files and the Go source, so nothing else belongs
# in the build context. Without this the whole working tree is sent to the daemon, which locally
# means bin/, builds/, vendor/ and .git as well.
#
# This excludes everything and then re-includes exactly what the Dockerfile copies, so adding a
# COPY without adding it here fails the build rather than quietly growing the context.
*

!go.mod
!go.sum
!main.go
!api
!pkg
